========================================================================================================
levels at each category's terminal quarter, 2020Q1=100. 'defect' is the
as-built/adjacent ratio; 'drift' is the adjacent/GEKS ratio.

cat          terminal  as-built  adjacent     GEKS  defect x  drift x  defect share
audio          2024Q4     637.3     555.4    396.7      1.15     1.40           29%
coding         2025Q1     492.4     273.7    312.8      1.80     0.88          129%
design         2024Q4     338.4     230.0    127.1      1.47     1.81           39%
marketing      2024Q4     798.2     398.2    282.2      2.00     1.41           67%
translation    2023Q1     144.7     168.2    200.0      0.86     0.84           46%
video          2024Q4     540.3     405.6    298.3      1.33     1.36           48%
writing        2024Q4     359.2     281.6    205.8      1.28     1.37           44%

  'defect x' > 1 means the as-built chain overstates relative to the same
  estimator with long links removed. 'drift x' > 1 is genuine chain drift.
  'defect share' is the fraction of the total log gap the defect explains.

