========================================================================================================
2. IS THE ELASTICITY REGRESSION SPURIOUS?
========================================================================================================

fitted on the AS-BUILT chained series, which is what the shipped table uses.
DW near 2 = no serial correlation; DW below ~1 = the OLS SE is not usable.

cat            n  beta(AI)   t OLS    t NW     DW   R2 AI  R2 time  R2 CPI  beta(CPI)  d-diff t
audio         20    -0.379   -8.93   -5.44   0.24   0.816    0.928   0.960       8.38      0.00
coding        21     0.380   13.75    7.67   0.50   0.909    0.974   0.939       5.95     -0.02
design        23     0.295    3.84    3.46   0.26   0.412    0.979   0.976       5.47      0.48
marketing     21     0.546   16.12   10.03   0.32   0.932    0.979   0.919       8.17      2.26
translation   14     0.095    3.74    4.97   0.92   0.539    0.463   0.344       1.30      0.06
writing       21     0.382   11.00    6.98   0.60   0.864    0.941   0.970       5.71      0.20

  READING:
   * 'R2 time' is a placebo — a linear trend has no AI content whatever.
     Where it matches or beats 'R2 AI', the AI score is proxying for time.
   * 'R2 CPI' / 'beta(CPI)' is a second placebo. CPI-U does not measure AI.
   * 't NW' is the OLS t corrected for serial correlation. The published
     table's p-values use the uncorrected one.
   * 'd-diff t' differences both sides. A common trend drops out; whatever
     survives is a relationship between the CHANGES.

